00:52:39.580 --> 00:52:43.170
My number six, in stark contrast,

00:52:43.170 --> 00:52:47.242
due to your last entry is the
Black Lives Matter movement.

00:52:47.242 --> 00:52:48.180
Okay.

00:52:48.180 --> 00:52:52.860
So yeah, I'm making a hard turn here

00:52:55.615 --> 00:52:59.677
into some meaningful and
potentially heavy waters.

00:53:05.364 --> 00:53:08.447
It's such a pivotal point in history.

00:53:09.340 --> 00:53:11.800
I actually still feel,

00:53:11.800 --> 00:53:15.860
whenever I start to talk about
it, I get really hesitant

00:53:15.860 --> 00:53:20.860
because I'm like, who
am I to talk about this?

00:53:21.500 --> 00:53:24.073
Or to figure out what to say.

00:53:24.073 --> 00:53:25.850
What if I say the wrong
thing or the right thing?

00:53:25.850 --> 00:53:28.120
There's still that residual
thing that's happening.

00:53:28.120 --> 00:53:33.120
But for me, it's learning
that you know what,

00:53:34.150 --> 00:53:35.483
I'm engaged in this.

00:53:36.890 --> 00:53:38.280
And this is not just something

00:53:38.280 --> 00:53:41.130
that I can hold at arms
length, further away,

00:53:41.130 --> 00:53:44.730
I need to look at these issues,
I need to become educated,

00:53:44.730 --> 00:53:46.340
that's what this year was

00:53:46.340 --> 00:53:51.340
in terms of me stopping
and paying more attention

00:53:54.330 --> 00:53:55.480
to the movement.

00:53:55.480 --> 00:53:58.280
And also, I just wanna give a shout out

00:53:58.280 --> 00:54:00.123
to all the mythical beasts who,

00:54:02.580 --> 00:54:04.520
we had a fundraiser early on,

00:54:04.520 --> 00:54:06.340
and then there was lots of donations

00:54:06.340 --> 00:54:08.510
made to a variety of charities

00:54:08.510 --> 00:54:10.150
associated with Black
Lives Matter movement.

00:54:10.150 --> 00:54:12.700
And it was extremely meaningful to me

00:54:17.499 --> 00:54:20.666
to do something and to make up my mind

00:54:25.330 --> 00:54:27.550
to be a force for good,

00:54:27.550 --> 00:54:32.323
and to try my best to
figure out how I do that.

00:54:33.160 --> 00:54:37.130
And whether that's as a
company or as an individual,

00:54:37.130 --> 00:54:39.820
and as a family, I think it's...

00:54:39.820 --> 00:54:41.980
And do I have it figured out?

00:54:41.980 --> 00:54:45.000
And am I tooting any type of horn?

00:54:45.000 --> 00:54:47.490
I certainly hope it doesn't seem like it.

00:54:47.490 --> 00:54:51.550
But I would be remiss if I
didn't put it on the list

00:54:51.550 --> 00:54:52.530
and say that...

00:54:52.530 --> 00:54:57.200
I mean, it was a pivotal
moment for me personally

00:54:57.200 --> 00:54:59.990
to have this level of interaction

00:55:00.904 --> 00:55:03.447
with Black Lives Matter and
such an important movement.

00:55:03.447 --> 00:55:06.300
And it also made my list in
a slightly different way.

00:55:06.300 --> 00:55:08.180
But I'll wait to share
that when I get there.

00:55:08.180 --> 00:55:09.530
But yeah, I think that...

00:55:11.520 --> 00:55:13.830
Yeah, this was a year

00:55:17.640 --> 00:55:18.473
to be clear,

00:55:19.904 --> 00:55:24.904
these issues have been things
that we personally cared about

00:55:26.667 --> 00:55:31.667
for quite a while, but
I think that there is,

00:55:32.010 --> 00:55:34.432
sometimes when you're like, why?

00:55:34.432 --> 00:55:37.540
Okay, step one is caring.

00:55:37.540 --> 00:55:38.817
Admitting that there is a problem,

00:55:38.817 --> 00:55:41.090
admitting that you might even be

00:55:41.090 --> 00:55:42.793
a part of the problem, right?

00:55:44.270 --> 00:55:49.270
Step two is doing something about it.

00:55:50.938 --> 00:55:53.830
And part of that has been being a student.

00:55:53.830 --> 00:55:55.280
Because again, like you said,

00:55:58.888 --> 00:56:01.250
we're not the ones with the ideas,

00:56:01.250 --> 00:56:06.250
we're in a position where
the things that we say,

00:56:06.370 --> 00:56:10.570
the things that we commit to
are impactful and powerful,

00:56:10.570 --> 00:56:11.540
that's a privilege.

00:56:11.540 --> 00:56:13.540
And I think that this is a year

00:56:13.540 --> 00:56:15.573
where being a student, reading books,

00:56:16.820 --> 00:56:19.560
people who have looked at these issues,

00:56:19.560 --> 00:56:23.090
black voices who have really
considered these things

00:56:23.090 --> 00:56:26.410
in a way that we could never
consider them personally,

00:56:26.410 --> 00:56:28.810
but being able to
appreciate that perspective

00:56:28.810 --> 00:56:31.010
and learn from it, and
kind of be a student.

00:56:34.741 --> 00:56:37.820
For me, this year kind
of represented going from

00:56:37.820 --> 00:56:41.250
being concerned and feeling like,

00:56:41.250 --> 00:56:43.660
yeah something needs to be done about this

00:56:43.660 --> 00:56:46.640
to begin to listen to people
who have been saying that

00:56:46.640 --> 00:56:48.450
and actually taking action for years,

00:56:48.450 --> 00:56:51.020
and saying, okay, how can we be supportive

00:56:51.020 --> 00:56:52.840
and be a part of that?

00:56:52.840 --> 00:56:53.730
And I'll talk a little bit more

00:56:53.730 --> 00:56:55.680
about a personal thing related to that.

00:56:57.030 --> 00:56:58.660
What's your number five?
This is one of my

00:56:58.660 --> 00:57:00.030
higher ones.

00:57:00.030 --> 00:57:04.770
Number five is the all day live stream

00:57:05.660 --> 00:57:07.760
that we did relatively recently.

00:57:07.760 --> 00:57:09.130
I mean, there has been some dispute

00:57:09.130 --> 00:57:12.280
over whether or not doing it
from 9:00 to 5:00 was all day,

00:57:12.280 --> 00:57:14.280
but for us, that was all day .

00:57:15.390 --> 00:57:17.850
But we didn't really know

00:57:17.850 --> 00:57:20.810
what we were getting
ourselves into with this.

00:57:20.810 --> 00:57:24.150
We did the live stream that
benefited Inner-City Arts,

00:57:24.150 --> 00:57:25.580
a charity that we had been wanting

00:57:25.580 --> 00:57:27.480
to partner with for a while

00:57:27.480 --> 00:57:29.600
and had not really, given
the nature of this year,

00:57:29.600 --> 00:57:31.350
been given an opportunity to do it.

00:57:33.100 --> 00:57:38.100
And people, influencers,
or whatever you wanna say

00:57:39.750 --> 00:57:42.670
doing charity live streams,
it's not a new thing,

00:57:42.670 --> 00:57:44.877
but it was new for us.

00:57:44.877 --> 00:57:46.640
And we were like, if we're gonna do this,

00:57:46.640 --> 00:57:48.990
we wanna do it in a way that's effective

00:57:48.990 --> 00:57:50.690
and actually makes a difference,

00:57:50.690 --> 00:57:53.090
but we wanna do it in
a way that's mythical.

00:57:53.090 --> 00:57:56.223
We wanna do it in a way
that is entertaining.

00:57:57.906 --> 00:58:01.800
And our team did an incredible job

00:58:01.800 --> 00:58:04.320
of pulling together the live stream.

00:58:04.320 --> 00:58:08.240
And then the mythical
beasts did an incredible job

00:58:08.240 --> 00:58:10.740
of showing up and giving.

00:58:10.740 --> 00:58:13.250
We raised over $350,000
for Inner-City Arts.

00:58:13.250 --> 00:58:14.083
Yeah, I was blown away.

00:58:14.083 --> 00:58:15.950
And I will say, you know
what, we're in alignment,

00:58:15.950 --> 00:58:17.530
this is my number five

00:58:17.530 --> 00:58:18.780
Oh, wow.
as well.

00:58:18.780 --> 00:58:19.613
Stars align.

00:58:21.201 --> 00:58:24.140
I went home that night after
the live stream had ended

00:58:24.140 --> 00:58:27.547
and I just was just processing.

00:58:27.547 --> 00:58:31.400
And every way that I
looked at the experience,

00:58:31.400 --> 00:58:35.820
if it was the work that
Inner-City Arts is doing

00:58:35.820 --> 00:58:39.920
and how I could just feel...

00:58:39.920 --> 00:58:43.480
I know what it feels like
to have to raise money

00:58:44.670 --> 00:58:46.390
as part of a nonprofit.

00:58:46.390 --> 00:58:50.140
And sometimes it feels very thankless.

00:58:50.140 --> 00:58:55.140
So, I got great joy from
knowing how it must've felt

00:58:56.250 --> 00:59:01.250
to the Inner-City Arts people
who dedicated their lives,

00:59:01.400 --> 00:59:05.370
and at times you might feel
under-appreciated or forgotten,

00:59:05.370 --> 00:59:06.860
to have that vote of confidence

00:59:06.860 --> 00:59:11.860
from people all over the
world was tremendously moving.

00:59:11.939 --> 00:59:15.880
Like you're saying, to look
at our team and to say how...

00:59:15.880 --> 00:59:17.580
It was within the context of their job,

00:59:17.580 --> 00:59:19.730
but I could tell that everyone involved

00:59:19.730 --> 00:59:22.440
went above and beyond
and outside of the scope

00:59:22.440 --> 00:59:26.050
of their normal work to give of themselves

00:59:26.050 --> 00:59:27.283
to make this happen.

00:59:28.930 --> 00:59:30.380
I got a lot of joy from that.

00:59:32.690 --> 00:59:37.290
Seeing our kids get involved,

00:59:37.290 --> 00:59:42.290
and calling our parents and
getting them involved in it

00:59:42.580 --> 00:59:47.580
and making a decision to
bring back former employees

00:59:47.610 --> 00:59:49.510
like Mike and Alex and Jen,

00:59:49.510 --> 00:59:53.353
and have them show up and celebrate,

00:59:54.980 --> 00:59:56.540
basically implied it like,

00:59:56.540 --> 00:59:59.250
you guys have moved on
from working with us,

00:59:59.250 --> 01:00:00.340
we're not employing you anymore,

01:00:00.340 --> 01:00:02.450
but you're still doing great
things out there in the world,

01:00:02.450 --> 01:00:05.130
and we still have this connection that...

01:00:05.130 --> 01:00:06.740
It felt good to still be connected

01:00:06.740 --> 01:00:09.750
and to bring them back in and
to have this extended family.

01:00:09.750 --> 01:00:12.080
But ultimately to make a decision

01:00:12.080 --> 01:00:14.430
that it was a family affair,

01:00:14.430 --> 01:00:18.793
I saw that one of the
comments afterward was,

01:00:20.150 --> 01:00:21.140
one mythical beast,

01:00:21.140 --> 01:00:24.997
I'm sorry I can't remember
your handle specifically said,

01:00:24.997 --> 01:00:27.110
"I love being a part of this family."

01:00:27.110 --> 01:00:30.450
Because we decided we
weren't gonna bring in guests

01:00:30.450 --> 01:00:33.300
and we weren't gonna make it one of those

01:00:33.300 --> 01:00:34.970
telethon type things, which is great,

01:00:34.970 --> 01:00:36.610
and we love being a part of that too,

01:00:36.610 --> 01:00:39.780
but for it to be our thing

01:00:39.780 --> 01:00:42.150
in partnership with Inner-City Arts

01:00:42.150 --> 01:00:46.467
was something that I
think, just like I said,

01:00:46.467 --> 01:00:47.610
and there's many more ways,

01:00:47.610 --> 01:00:50.100
but every way I would
look at it from any angle,

01:00:50.100 --> 01:00:54.370
it was just something
that brought a lot of joy

01:00:57.160 --> 01:01:01.970
to invest in something in the arts.

01:01:01.970 --> 01:01:04.330
Well, it was kinda
mythically coming full circle

01:01:04.330 --> 01:01:07.883
because we're doing something
that we're having fun doing,

01:01:07.883 --> 01:01:10.900
it's entertaining, there's a
lot of lighthearted moments

01:01:10.900 --> 01:01:12.160
and fun moments,

01:01:12.160 --> 01:01:14.933
but it's directly doing
something for good.

01:01:15.870 --> 01:01:17.810
There's a lot of indirect good

01:01:17.810 --> 01:01:19.243
that we hear comes from
the stuff that we do,

01:01:19.243 --> 01:01:21.280
where it's like, oh, this
helped me get through

01:01:21.280 --> 01:01:22.430
a difficult time or whatever,

01:01:22.430 --> 01:01:24.480
and of course we do give to charity,

01:01:24.480 --> 01:01:27.450
but to do something
that is so directly tied

01:01:27.450 --> 01:01:30.300
to a course like that,
it felt really good.

01:01:30.300 --> 01:01:32.110
That's why it was my number five too, man.

01:01:32.110 --> 01:01:33.590
So, you're number four.

01:01:33.590 --> 01:01:35.600
Number four, okay.

