But was it one of your
top 10 favorite things?

01:02:37.080 --> 01:02:37.913
No.

01:02:39.165 --> 01:02:40.650
Because it's not on my list.

01:02:40.650 --> 01:02:42.160
I mean again-

01:02:42.160 --> 01:02:43.280
Well, my number four, man.

01:02:43.280 --> 01:02:44.870
The order...
Doesn't matter?

01:02:44.870 --> 01:02:46.030
It could be on my list.

01:02:46.030 --> 01:02:50.350
I mean, my trip to Joshua Tree

01:02:51.760 --> 01:02:52.733
isn't on the list.

01:02:53.640 --> 01:02:55.040
My beach trip isn't on the list,

01:02:55.040 --> 01:02:56.940
but there's like, they should be.

01:02:56.940 --> 01:02:58.773
Yeah. The list can only be so big.

01:02:59.740 --> 01:03:01.810
My number four is

01:03:04.930 --> 01:03:09.103
starting and doing the
listening party with Britney.

01:03:10.870 --> 01:03:12.330
Yeah, that's my number three too.

01:03:12.330 --> 01:03:14.943
No, it isn't.

01:03:17.480 --> 01:03:18.313
It's not.

01:03:18.313 --> 01:03:20.730
Britney lived with us all last year.

01:03:20.730 --> 01:03:23.103
He made my top 10 last year.

01:03:24.220 --> 01:03:25.830
And then he moved out,

01:03:25.830 --> 01:03:27.720
and especially with
quarantine being shut down,

01:03:27.720 --> 01:03:29.500
it's like, we didn't see each other.

01:03:29.500 --> 01:03:31.410
And actually, we kind
of fell out of touch.

01:03:31.410 --> 01:03:32.243
Didn't like each other any more.

01:03:32.243 --> 01:03:35.730
Even though he lived, he's
just over there in Burbank,

01:03:35.730 --> 01:03:38.140
he's not far away, but
we couldn't get together.

01:03:38.140 --> 01:03:39.021
Right.

01:03:39.021 --> 01:03:43.330
And so, one day I'm like, I
need to reconnect with him,

01:03:43.330 --> 01:03:44.163
and we were talking

01:03:44.163 --> 01:03:47.020
and I was like talking about how I missed,

01:03:47.020 --> 01:03:48.140
we started talking about
music and I was like,

01:03:48.140 --> 01:03:49.223
you know what?

01:03:50.850 --> 01:03:52.620
I miss us talking about music.

01:03:52.620 --> 01:03:55.210
That's what we would
stay up late at night,

01:03:55.210 --> 01:03:57.710
just like standing around
in the kitchen just talking,

01:03:57.710 --> 01:03:58.880
you know how he is.

01:03:58.880 --> 01:04:00.010
You get him talking about music,

01:04:00.010 --> 01:04:01.420
He'll keep talking.
three hours later,

01:04:01.420 --> 01:04:02.720
you're still talking about music.

01:04:02.720 --> 01:04:04.430
And we would just play
songs for each other.

01:04:04.430 --> 01:04:05.650
He's an encyclopedia.

01:04:05.650 --> 01:04:08.000
We play songs for each other

01:04:08.000 --> 01:04:10.210
and I was like, you know what, let's...

01:04:10.210 --> 01:04:11.233
And I'm just looking for things

01:04:11.233 --> 01:04:16.233
that become connection
amidst this COVID thing.

01:04:17.320 --> 01:04:19.740
And I wanted to reconnect and I'm like,

01:04:19.740 --> 01:04:22.370
let's start making playlist,

01:04:22.370 --> 01:04:24.820
let's collaborate on a playlist.

01:04:24.820 --> 01:04:27.710
And that can be a way
that we can have a project

01:04:27.710 --> 01:04:29.740
and we can be talking to each other.

01:04:29.740 --> 01:04:31.960
And then we were like, screw it,

01:04:31.960 --> 01:04:34.220
let's do it on Instagram.

01:04:34.220 --> 01:04:37.210
If John Mayer can have an Instagram live,

01:04:37.210 --> 01:04:38.043
Yeah, anybody can.

01:04:38.043 --> 01:04:40.470
and that almost made the list,

01:04:40.470 --> 01:04:42.010
me and Lilly watching "Current Mood"

01:04:42.010 --> 01:04:44.440
where we were obsessed with
that until he stopped doing it.

01:04:44.440 --> 01:04:47.090
Yeah. It became an
obligation for him too .

01:04:48.740 --> 01:04:49.690
I was like, we can do that.

01:04:49.690 --> 01:04:52.510
So, we made it a live stream,

01:04:52.510 --> 01:04:55.420
but it was very much about
the two of us connecting,

01:04:55.420 --> 01:04:57.640
and anybody who wanted
to share on that music,

01:04:57.640 --> 01:05:01.460
they could do it, and
still can on my Instagram.

01:05:01.460 --> 01:05:06.193
But it was a very special time for us,

01:05:07.130 --> 01:05:08.720
'cause we would talk throughout the week

01:05:08.720 --> 01:05:11.070
and get a kick out of
building this playlist.

01:05:11.070 --> 01:05:13.960
And then we would experience it together

01:05:13.960 --> 01:05:14.960
on this live stream.

01:05:14.960 --> 01:05:18.080
And especially early on,

01:05:18.080 --> 01:05:20.833
it was just an opportunity
for us to process,

01:05:22.680 --> 01:05:27.350
many times, the emotions of
going through quarantine.

01:05:27.350 --> 01:05:31.663
And because music is so
important to both of us,

01:05:32.870 --> 01:05:35.010
there's this really experience in

01:05:38.080 --> 01:05:41.773
the soul connection
that music can provide.

01:05:43.440 --> 01:05:45.080
Connecting to your own soul,

01:05:45.080 --> 01:05:47.230
but then also connecting to somebody else.

01:05:47.230 --> 01:05:52.230
And I mean, it bonded us at
a time when our relationship

01:05:53.735 --> 01:05:56.730
could have moved further apart.

01:05:56.730 --> 01:06:00.333
I find it interesting that at this point,

01:06:03.610 --> 01:06:05.750
the way that I approach things,

01:06:05.750 --> 01:06:07.920
I started to approach it very like,

01:06:07.920 --> 01:06:09.860
okay, well, this is how we gotta do it,

01:06:09.860 --> 01:06:11.724
and this is what it's about.

01:06:11.724 --> 01:06:13.537
And I started making it
about the wrong things.

01:06:13.537 --> 01:06:16.450
And I was like, hey, I need
to take a break from this

01:06:16.450 --> 01:06:19.070
because things are getting
busy here at work again.

01:06:19.070 --> 01:06:22.343
So, for like November,
we took a break from it.

01:06:24.090 --> 01:06:28.130
Because it started becoming
about something else

01:06:28.130 --> 01:06:31.210
and about an obligation to somebody

01:06:31.210 --> 01:06:33.990
besides just me and Britney hanging out.

01:06:33.990 --> 01:06:36.480
Yeah, things don't have
to last forever, man.

01:06:36.480 --> 01:06:38.280
Things don't have to last forever.

01:06:42.800 --> 01:06:44.750
There were a handful of lifelines

01:06:44.750 --> 01:06:46.910
that have gotten me through,

01:06:46.910 --> 01:06:48.340
and that was certainly one of them.

01:06:48.340 --> 01:06:52.957
And will always be very special to me.

01:06:52.957 --> 01:06:54.560
And I know, to him too.

01:06:54.560 --> 01:06:56.543
We had a lot of big laughs too.

01:06:57.890 --> 01:06:59.803
You know those big laughs?

01:07:00.800 --> 01:07:03.950
The laughs that come in the midst of

01:07:03.950 --> 01:07:06.928
when you just feel like crap.

01:07:06.928 --> 01:07:10.940
I mean, there's few
things more therapeutic.

01:07:10.940 --> 01:07:13.960
Maybe there's nothing more
therapeutic than a good laugh

01:07:13.960 --> 01:07:16.090
at the right time when you really need it.

01:07:16.090 --> 01:07:18.533
And so, that's what a listening party.

01:07:19.521 --> 01:07:23.067
That's the soul of that for me.

01:07:23.067 --> 01:07:24.423
And that's my number four.

01:07:25.460 --> 01:07:27.610
My number three is related

01:07:27.610 --> 01:07:30.573
to the Black Lives Matter movement.

01:07:31.570 --> 01:07:36.110
And when everything was happening

01:07:37.390 --> 01:07:41.417
and specifically kind of the catalyst that

01:07:45.560 --> 01:07:48.770
just brought this issue
to the forefront again

01:07:48.770 --> 01:07:51.063
was the murder of George Floyd, right?

01:07:52.026 --> 01:07:57.026
And there's been a few times
when I've written something on,

01:07:58.640 --> 01:08:00.450
I'll write a medium
article about something,

01:08:00.450 --> 01:08:03.510
and usually the thing
that gets me to the point

01:08:03.510 --> 01:08:05.700
where I feel like I have something to say

01:08:05.700 --> 01:08:08.800
or there's something I have
to say that I can't not say

01:08:10.090 --> 01:08:14.863
is when I just see people
saying things online

01:08:18.470 --> 01:08:21.160
and I'm just like, I kinda feel
like I can speak into this.

01:08:21.160 --> 01:08:26.160
And I get something in
my mind and my heart

01:08:26.320 --> 01:08:29.323
and I just have to say it, I
have to just get it out, right?

01:08:33.248 --> 01:08:34.913
When everything was coming out,

01:08:38.670 --> 01:08:42.760
most people who have a
senior sort of public persona

01:08:42.760 --> 01:08:47.133
were acknowledging the
movement in some way, right?

01:08:48.010 --> 01:08:51.300
And for the same reasons
that you were pointing out

01:08:51.300 --> 01:08:52.700
in the beginning, it's just like,

01:08:52.700 --> 01:08:56.640
well, it seems to me that a lot of times,

01:08:56.640 --> 01:08:58.010
I'm not speaking for all white guys,

01:08:58.010 --> 01:09:00.590
but it tends to be kind
of a white guy thing

01:09:00.590 --> 01:09:02.520
to be like, well, I've
got something to say

01:09:02.520 --> 01:09:04.650
and you should listen to me, right?

01:09:04.650 --> 01:09:07.800
Anybody can do it, but we
have a pretty bad track record

01:09:07.800 --> 01:09:09.200
of believing that whatever we have to say

01:09:09.200 --> 01:09:10.950
is the most important thing to say.

01:09:11.950 --> 01:09:14.120
And so, I was sensitive to that,

01:09:14.120 --> 01:09:16.500
knowing that I don't
bring a lot of education

01:09:16.500 --> 01:09:18.940
and a lot of personal
experience and perspective

01:09:18.940 --> 01:09:20.020
into this issue.

01:09:20.020 --> 01:09:22.590
So again, I was like, I want to listen,

01:09:22.590 --> 01:09:25.450
but I also want to be a responsible ally.

01:09:29.350 --> 01:09:33.230
And it hit me that the way
that I could be involved was,

01:09:33.230 --> 01:09:35.850
I saw a lot of people saying things

01:09:35.850 --> 01:09:40.180
related to the incident with George Floyd

01:09:40.180 --> 01:09:43.550
that sort of reflected some
things that I might have said

01:09:44.520 --> 01:09:49.520
in my past that are kind of
based on where I come from

01:09:49.630 --> 01:09:53.230
and the mentality that I had growing up,

01:09:53.230 --> 01:09:55.130
and kind of the lack of experience

01:09:55.130 --> 01:09:56.890
and lack of knowledge that I had,

01:09:56.890 --> 01:09:59.170
and lack of empathy, frankly,

01:09:59.170 --> 01:10:01.720
that I had for people
outside of my own experience.

01:10:03.350 --> 01:10:04.567
And so, that's when I wrote what I call

01:10:04.567 --> 01:10:05.900
"Letter to a White Man",

01:10:05.900 --> 01:10:08.920
which was essentially writing
a letter to the old RET

01:10:08.920 --> 01:10:11.460
and saying, "Hey, listen, I
know that you actually do care

01:10:11.460 --> 01:10:12.293
about these things,

01:10:12.293 --> 01:10:14.380
but a lot of the things
that you think and say

01:10:14.380 --> 01:10:17.420
and the way that you react to these things

01:10:17.420 --> 01:10:18.810
are contributing to the problem,

01:10:18.810 --> 01:10:20.910
they're not actually solving the problem."

01:10:21.850 --> 01:10:25.520
So, I wrote that kind of
self-conscious about it again,

01:10:25.520 --> 01:10:28.130
because it was ironically a
white dude saying something.

01:10:28.130 --> 01:10:29.670
But again, I was a white
dude saying something

01:10:29.670 --> 01:10:31.253
to a white dude,

01:10:32.880 --> 01:10:35.340
and my former self to be specific.

01:10:35.340 --> 01:10:37.100
And the thing that was
really encouraging about it

01:10:37.100 --> 01:10:39.770
was the response.

01:10:39.770 --> 01:10:43.860
I mean, sure, a lot of
people were upset with me,

01:10:43.860 --> 01:10:46.000
pointed out all the
things that they thought,

01:10:46.000 --> 01:10:47.210
all the places where I was wrong

01:10:47.210 --> 01:10:52.210
but there were a number of
people who communicated,

01:10:53.050 --> 01:10:55.030
whether it be through
like an Instagram message

01:10:55.030 --> 01:10:56.820
or something on Twitter,

01:10:56.820 --> 01:11:01.820
who said, "Hey, this was
legitimately impacted me.

01:11:03.600 --> 01:11:05.470
Because a lot of the things that you said

01:11:05.470 --> 01:11:07.487
are the things that I have
been thinking about this,

01:11:07.487 --> 01:11:12.110
and it actually gave me a
chance to reflect on that

01:11:12.110 --> 01:11:15.200
and to consider a different perspective."

01:11:15.200 --> 01:11:20.200
And just one person saying
that would have been worth it.

01:11:20.340 --> 01:11:23.593
But the reaction was super positive.

01:11:26.480 --> 01:11:31.480
For me, I wasn't doing it for attention,

01:11:31.580 --> 01:11:35.160
and I wasn't doing it to
get a pat on the back,

01:11:35.160 --> 01:11:36.610
I was doing it simply because I know

01:11:36.610 --> 01:11:39.410
there was a lot of people
out there like me, right?

01:11:39.410 --> 01:11:42.285
And I thought I had
something to say to me.

01:11:42.285 --> 01:11:45.850
And the fact that-
And to hear from some people

01:11:45.850 --> 01:11:50.740
Yeah.
like that,

01:11:50.740 --> 01:11:52.030
that was your aim.

01:11:52.030 --> 01:11:53.340
Yeah.

01:11:53.340 --> 01:11:56.780
So, that was super, super encouraging.

01:11:56.780 --> 01:11:58.420
So, I bet that felt good.

01:11:58.420 --> 01:12:01.160
'Cause it's the same reason

01:12:01.160 --> 01:12:04.600
that the live stream is on the list.

01:12:04.600 --> 01:12:05.433
Because it's

01:12:10.930 --> 01:12:13.883
realizing that we do have a platform.

01:12:14.918 --> 01:12:17.610
And again, that pervasive question of,

01:12:17.610 --> 01:12:19.330
what's the right thing to do

01:12:19.330 --> 01:12:21.720
with this opportunity that we have?

01:12:21.720 --> 01:12:25.163
And you've got things that you wanna say,

01:12:27.830 --> 01:12:29.880
it can be a treacherous path to figure out

01:12:29.880 --> 01:12:33.750
how to take a stand on issues
or how to make a difference.

01:12:33.750 --> 01:12:38.500
And you can be intimidated
into doing nothing,

01:12:38.500 --> 01:12:42.463
even within your own mind,
not by anyone else, even.

01:12:44.090 --> 01:12:48.570
So, I mean that's something that

01:12:51.280 --> 01:12:53.710
been inspired by with the
Black Lives Matter Movement,

01:12:53.710 --> 01:12:58.710
is that you can find
a way to do something.

01:13:01.680 --> 01:13:05.100
And yeah, I'm super
proud of what you wrote,

01:13:05.100 --> 01:13:07.230
and how you went about it.

01:13:07.230 --> 01:13:09.199
And it's also not on my list.

01:13:12.270 --> 01:13:13.720
Well, thanks.

01:13:13.720 --> 01:13:15.993
My number three is a painful one,

01:13:19.510 --> 01:13:21.560
I might cry, I don't know
exactly what I'm gonna say,

01:13:21.560 --> 01:13:23.500
so I just feel emotional about it.

01:13:23.500 --> 01:13:25.300
But I wanted to put this on the list again

01:13:25.300 --> 01:13:30.300
because it was an impactful
moment for me this year.

01:13:35.463 --> 01:13:38.170
And maybe there's a silver lining to it,

01:13:38.170 --> 01:13:42.200
but it's just something
that I haven't talked about,

01:13:42.200 --> 01:13:47.200
but was a defining moment in my 2020.

01:13:47.300 --> 01:13:51.800
And that is that when my grandma,

01:13:51.800 --> 01:13:56.800
who I've always called my nanny,
my mom's mom, passed away.

01:13:56.850 --> 01:14:01.717
She passed away in June
and I couldn't go home.

01:14:03.610 --> 01:14:04.520
Right.

01:14:04.520 --> 01:14:07.070
And it hurt a lot.

01:14:07.070 --> 01:14:08.683
And it still hurts.

01:14:14.771 --> 01:14:15.604
It wasn't a surprise,

01:14:20.904 --> 01:14:22.810
it didn't happen quickly,

01:14:22.810 --> 01:14:27.743
and in some ways, that made
it much more difficult.

01:14:31.540 --> 01:14:33.667
I was looking back at my Evernotes,

01:14:35.980 --> 01:14:37.270
which sometimes they're dated,

01:14:37.270 --> 01:14:38.970
but it's definitely not a journal,

01:14:41.170 --> 01:14:46.170
of my record of my memories
from Thanksgiving last year.

01:14:47.640 --> 01:14:50.793
And I was like,

01:14:51.790 --> 01:14:52.960
who was here this Thanksgiving

01:14:52.960 --> 01:14:54.580
and is not gonna be
here next Thanksgiving?

01:14:54.580 --> 01:14:57.890
And I was thinking about nanny,
when you go and visit her,

01:14:57.890 --> 01:15:00.810
and I think I talked
about that experience.

01:15:00.810 --> 01:15:03.140
Every year you go home as
your grandparents get older,

01:15:03.140 --> 01:15:05.420
it's like, maybe this is the
last year I'm spending with her

01:15:05.420 --> 01:15:07.300
and living in California.

01:15:07.300 --> 01:15:11.340
Maybe this is the last time
I'm seeing her in person.

01:15:11.340 --> 01:15:12.490
Right.

01:15:12.490 --> 01:15:13.760
Was that Thanksgiving.

01:15:13.760 --> 01:15:16.750
And it turns out that it was in.

01:15:16.750 --> 01:15:18.770
So, it is nice to have that awareness

01:15:18.770 --> 01:15:21.520
and to have those memories of,

01:15:21.520 --> 01:15:26.520
this may be it so I'm
going to acknowledge that.

01:15:29.180 --> 01:15:33.350
And so, I'm grateful for that.

01:15:33.350 --> 01:15:36.063
The last time I saw her in person was,

01:15:37.260 --> 01:15:40.710
there was kind of an understanding
that that might be it.

01:15:40.710 --> 01:15:42.280
I will say that it was that way

01:15:42.280 --> 01:15:43.933
for a couple of years, actually.

01:15:45.930 --> 01:15:47.253
And she was at home,

01:15:50.270 --> 01:15:51.670
and they brought an hospice,

01:15:54.498 --> 01:15:58.020
she was made comfortable as she passed.

01:16:00.874 --> 01:16:03.100
And that was about a week and a half.

01:16:03.100 --> 01:16:08.100
And it was excruciatingly
difficult to come to grips

01:16:08.660 --> 01:16:12.300
with the fact that the right decision

01:16:12.300 --> 01:16:15.743
was not to fly home at that time.

01:16:16.670 --> 01:16:21.040
It wasn't simply just the COVID of it all,

01:16:21.040 --> 01:16:22.930
I mean, there were a number of factors

01:16:22.930 --> 01:16:27.930
which impacted my immediate family.

01:16:31.180 --> 01:16:32.150
I'll just say that

01:16:34.330 --> 01:16:37.720
the accumulation of all the factors

01:16:37.720 --> 01:16:39.440
led to it being the right decision,

01:16:39.440 --> 01:16:41.533
but it's like, there's still
this doubt in your mind

01:16:41.533 --> 01:16:44.960
just like, should I go home or not?

01:16:44.960 --> 01:16:48.860
And it's like, it never felt great.

01:16:48.860 --> 01:16:50.650
It still doesn't feel great.

01:16:50.650 --> 01:16:52.460
In some ways, it doesn't feel real,

01:16:52.460 --> 01:16:54.603
still having not been home,

01:17:02.447 --> 01:17:04.927
I haven't had the experience
of going back in the house

01:17:04.927 --> 01:17:06.283
and her not being there.

01:17:13.450 --> 01:17:14.950
I know a lot of people...

01:17:14.950 --> 01:17:17.520
She didn't have COVID,
just as a side note,

01:17:17.520 --> 01:17:20.560
but I know a lot of people
have lost a lot of loved ones

01:17:20.560 --> 01:17:25.560
and it has been extremely painful
to not be able to see them

01:17:25.570 --> 01:17:26.823
as they're passing.

01:17:28.000 --> 01:17:29.910
But they're right there.

01:17:29.910 --> 01:17:32.290
I was across the country
and it was excruciating.

01:17:32.290 --> 01:17:33.960
So, my heart goes out to all those people

01:17:33.960 --> 01:17:37.370
who are on the other
side of a pane of glass,

01:17:37.370 --> 01:17:40.253
having to watch someone pass.

01:17:45.880 --> 01:17:48.910
I knew that I would have
spoken at her funeral.

01:17:48.910 --> 01:17:53.910
And when she was planning her funeral,

01:17:57.910 --> 01:18:00.913
she was telling her sisters
what she wanted to wear,

01:18:02.100 --> 01:18:03.083
and she said,

01:18:04.227 --> 01:18:07.080
"I want Link to sing a
song at the funeral."

01:18:07.080 --> 01:18:11.020
And I don't think she quite understood

01:18:11.020 --> 01:18:14.270
that I wasn't gonna be able to be there.

01:18:14.270 --> 01:18:17.420
And so, it broke my heart to know that

01:18:20.880 --> 01:18:22.510
I couldn't deliver on that.

01:18:24.200 --> 01:18:25.520
But I wrote a eulogy

01:18:28.114 --> 01:18:31.210
and I emailed it to the to the pastor

01:18:31.210 --> 01:18:35.910
who was already speaking,
to read at the funeral.

01:18:35.910 --> 01:18:38.900
And I had mailed them

01:18:40.570 --> 01:18:43.270
the record that we made
for the Mythical Society

01:18:43.270 --> 01:18:47.013
where we covered "Silver
Wings", the Merle Haggard song.

01:18:48.090 --> 01:18:51.190
And I knew it was my aunt, Vickie,

01:18:51.190 --> 01:18:55.970
who, for basically her entire adult life,

01:18:55.970 --> 01:18:58.500
lived with my nanny.

01:18:58.500 --> 01:19:01.360
Oldest sister, youngest
sister lived together.

01:19:01.360 --> 01:19:05.780
Even when my papa was alive,
aunt Vicki still lived there.

01:19:05.780 --> 01:19:08.090
And then when he passed, it
was just the two of them.

01:19:08.090 --> 01:19:09.720
And now it's just aunt Vicki,

01:19:09.720 --> 01:19:11.493
and she has another sister
that she's close with

01:19:11.493 --> 01:19:14.010
and spends a lot of time
with, thank goodness.

01:19:14.010 --> 01:19:16.170
But I mailed them the record

01:19:16.170 --> 01:19:17.430
because it was her favorite song

01:19:17.430 --> 01:19:20.190
but then that was the solution.

01:19:20.190 --> 01:19:23.283
They actually played our-

01:19:24.535 --> 01:19:27.800
Yeah, they played our
rendition of "Silver Wings"

01:19:27.800 --> 01:19:29.110
at the funeral service.

01:19:29.110 --> 01:19:31.873
And then they read my eulogy.

01:19:33.320 --> 01:19:38.320
But it was just tough not to be there.

01:19:46.510 --> 01:19:49.330
So, there's a lot of
pain associated with it

01:19:49.330 --> 01:19:52.763
and a lack of closure.

01:19:55.770 --> 01:19:58.660
I think until I can get back home again,

01:19:58.660 --> 01:20:00.553
I think it'll still kind of be in,

01:20:03.370 --> 01:20:08.370
the wound will be a little
more open than I would help.

01:20:12.010 --> 01:20:12.890
It's my number three

01:20:12.890 --> 01:20:16.633
because it's such a poignant milestone,

01:20:21.060 --> 01:20:22.490
I don't know how it's changed me,

01:20:22.490 --> 01:20:24.390
but you can just feel that like, okay,

01:20:25.346 --> 01:20:27.540
this is one of those things
that shapes you as a person

01:20:27.540 --> 01:20:28.640
when you go through something,

01:20:28.640 --> 01:20:30.640
when it's so frustrating and so painful

01:20:30.640 --> 01:20:33.733
to not be able to be
there for your family.

01:20:36.180 --> 01:20:37.454
Well, it's not on my list.

01:20:39.110 --> 01:20:40.313
But thanks for sharing.

01:20:42.600 --> 01:20:45.344
I have one that probably is on your list.

01:20:45.344 --> 01:20:48.113
And that is my number two.

01:20:49.850 --> 01:20:54.850
Us telling our stories the last
years on this very podcast,

01:20:55.400 --> 01:20:58.500
which I guess we did in January, February?

01:20:58.500 --> 01:20:59.550
We did it...

01:21:00.670 --> 01:21:03.946
Yup, I mean, in January, the
first two episodes came out

01:21:03.946 --> 01:21:04.840
and then in February
And then February.

01:21:04.840 --> 01:21:07.670
is when your deconstruction
story came out then mine.

01:21:07.670 --> 01:21:08.580
So, it's January
Yeah, 'cause we kind of

01:21:08.580 --> 01:21:09.413
to February.
toggle back on everything.

01:21:09.413 --> 01:21:11.340
And this is my number two as well.

01:21:11.340 --> 01:21:13.100
Okay, we sync up again.
So,

01:21:13.100 --> 01:21:14.543
we're syncing up once again.

01:21:16.760 --> 01:21:19.860
I don't think, boy, what a weird year,

01:21:19.860 --> 01:21:22.890
what a very, very weird year

01:21:22.890 --> 01:21:26.240
that this happened this year
and then COVID happened.

01:21:26.240 --> 01:21:27.073
But-

01:21:27.073 --> 01:21:30.370
I think we had decided
we were gonna do this

01:21:30.370 --> 01:21:31.270
At the end of 2019.

01:21:31.270 --> 01:21:33.920
October or November of 2019.
Yeah. Yeah.

01:21:33.920 --> 01:21:37.240
And so, we had the sense
that it was gonna be like,

01:21:37.240 --> 01:21:40.090
we're doing it early in 2020,
but it was gonna be something

01:21:40.090 --> 01:21:44.840
that would maybe reshape
the course of "Ear Biscuits"

01:21:44.840 --> 01:21:47.130
or we didn't know it would lead to.

01:21:47.130 --> 01:21:50.417
I was antsy to tell the story, right?

01:21:50.417 --> 01:21:52.850
And I think that for me,

01:21:52.850 --> 01:21:54.850
it had been kind of a long time coming.

01:21:54.850 --> 01:21:58.820
And one of the reasons I wanted
to kind of tell our story

01:22:00.410 --> 01:22:05.410
is because our background
of growing up as Christians,

01:22:06.310 --> 01:22:09.550
not just Christians but
evangelical Christians

01:22:09.550 --> 01:22:13.200
it was the center piece of our life,

01:22:13.200 --> 01:22:16.203
and then the centerpiece of
our career in the early days.

01:22:19.510 --> 01:22:24.510
There was so much tension in
being vulnerable and personal,

01:22:26.480 --> 01:22:28.203
and talking about our lives,

01:22:29.539 --> 01:22:32.610
mostly in this medium of "Ear Biscuits",

01:22:32.610 --> 01:22:34.610
but we talk about ourselves all the time.

01:22:34.610 --> 01:22:37.130
We're constantly kind of
telling the stories and stuff,

01:22:37.130 --> 01:22:41.110
and to have this giant piece of your past

01:22:41.110 --> 01:22:43.330
that informs who you are

01:22:43.330 --> 01:22:46.183
and constantly finding
ways to gloss over it,

01:22:47.290 --> 01:22:49.170
there were so many tangential things

01:22:51.300 --> 01:22:53.707
about our career and the
path that we're at right now,

01:22:53.707 --> 01:22:57.680
and the fact that we worked
with campus crusade for a while

01:22:57.680 --> 01:23:00.010
and it's kind of the reason
that we got into comedy,

01:23:00.010 --> 01:23:01.950
all these things that
we weren't able to say,

01:23:01.950 --> 01:23:05.280
to me, there was always
this like kind of shame

01:23:05.280 --> 01:23:07.770
associated with our past,

01:23:07.770 --> 01:23:11.570
but also a shame of not
being honest about it

01:23:11.570 --> 01:23:14.580
that had just created this tension.

01:23:14.580 --> 01:23:17.720
For me, telling the story

01:23:17.720 --> 01:23:22.720
and kind of just saying, here
it is, without any apologies,

01:23:23.010 --> 01:23:25.640
we're just gonna tell you the whole story

01:23:25.640 --> 01:23:28.883
of where we were and where we
are now and how we got here,

01:23:30.010 --> 01:23:35.003
to me, it opened something
up within me, right?

01:23:38.640 --> 01:23:40.030
The way that I think about

01:23:41.580 --> 01:23:43.377
the things that we talk
about on this podcast now

01:23:43.377 --> 01:23:46.550
has kind of changed pretty
dramatically for me.

01:23:46.550 --> 01:23:48.650
It's like, if there's something
that comes up and it's...

01:23:48.650 --> 01:23:52.680
We would avoid anything
that got into spirituality

01:23:52.680 --> 01:23:53.560
at all, right?

01:23:53.560 --> 01:23:55.490
If it was just like, well,
this kind of gets into talking

01:23:55.490 --> 01:23:57.773
about God or religion
or faith or whatever,

01:23:58.640 --> 01:23:59.473
we would avoid it.

01:23:59.473 --> 01:24:01.530
And it's so strange for people who,

01:24:01.530 --> 01:24:03.730
that is such a big part of who we are,

01:24:03.730 --> 01:24:05.330
to not be able to talk about it.

01:24:07.300 --> 01:24:09.480
I'm not even really gonna get into the...

01:24:09.480 --> 01:24:12.110
I mean, the response was overwhelming

01:24:12.110 --> 01:24:14.560
in every sense of the word,
both positive and negative,

01:24:14.560 --> 01:24:18.800
and the way that it kind of
transformed people's perspective

01:24:18.800 --> 01:24:21.820
of us, both for the good and for the bad,

01:24:21.820 --> 01:24:23.883
we gained fans, we lost fans.

01:24:25.510 --> 01:24:28.530
But really it was so impactful for me

01:24:28.530 --> 01:24:30.290
'cause I just felt like it was this,

01:24:30.290 --> 01:24:33.300
ironically, is the way that you describe

01:24:33.300 --> 01:24:34.970
becoming a Christian a lot of times,

01:24:34.970 --> 01:24:36.990
as a huge burden is lifted off of you.

01:24:36.990 --> 01:24:39.620
And you have this feeling,
this sense of relief

01:24:39.620 --> 01:24:42.593
when you give your life to God.

01:24:44.110 --> 01:24:46.760
Ironically for me, kind
of talking about how

01:24:48.030 --> 01:24:49.670
I'm in a completely different place

01:24:49.670 --> 01:24:52.180
and no longer consider myself a Christian

01:24:52.180 --> 01:24:54.480
or a person of faith in
that way specifically,

01:24:55.585 --> 01:24:57.940
was a huge burden that
was lifted off of me.

01:24:57.940 --> 01:25:00.490
I think for me, it was a
milestone in my spiritual journey

01:25:00.490 --> 01:25:04.990
because in a lot of ways,
it said, okay, now I can...

01:25:06.330 --> 01:25:07.820
Not that I couldn't move forward

01:25:07.820 --> 01:25:10.430
or I needed to talk about
it in order to move forward,

01:25:10.430 --> 01:25:15.430
but it kind of was that.

01:25:16.520 --> 01:25:19.550
I don't know, it was like,

01:25:19.550 --> 01:25:22.110
okay, I can document what
brought me to this point

01:25:22.110 --> 01:25:25.887
in my spiritual journey, the
exercise of talking about it

01:25:25.887 --> 01:25:27.450
and the preparation leading to that

01:25:27.450 --> 01:25:29.610
really helped me make
sense of it for myself

01:25:29.610 --> 01:25:31.150
so that now I can...

01:25:34.070 --> 01:25:35.870
It made it so I could move forward

01:25:35.870 --> 01:25:37.390
in a way that I don't think I could

01:25:37.390 --> 01:25:41.350
because I hadn't processed it enough.

01:25:41.350 --> 01:25:46.350
I mean, I definitely really began

01:25:46.800 --> 01:25:49.703
to appreciate my relationship with guilt.

01:25:50.640 --> 01:25:55.583
And this was the year
that I started therapy,

01:26:01.100 --> 01:26:03.950
and I'm continuing my spiritual journey.

01:26:03.950 --> 01:26:08.530
And a journey of openness
and self discovery

01:26:10.970 --> 01:26:12.090
as part of that too.

01:26:12.090 --> 01:26:17.090
But I'm moving forward in openness,

01:26:17.530 --> 01:26:21.300
and I'm also saying, all right,
I'm still coming to grips

01:26:21.300 --> 01:26:24.303
with, what is my relationship to guilt?

01:26:25.920 --> 01:26:29.940
In addition to what is
my relationship to God

01:26:29.940 --> 01:26:34.170
and to belief and expectations

01:26:35.484 --> 01:26:39.397
as a human or as a father or a husband.

01:26:40.480 --> 01:26:42.700
So again, these are all things

01:26:42.700 --> 01:26:45.850
that I'm still very much in process.

01:26:45.850 --> 01:26:48.870
I mean, who's not in process?

01:26:48.870 --> 01:26:53.870
But I do feel like it
released me in some ways,

01:26:55.170 --> 01:26:59.993
and then gave me a trajectory
to continue to move forward.

01:27:00.910 --> 01:27:02.800
So, it's not about a label,

01:27:02.800 --> 01:27:07.670
it's not about coming to a
conclusion or a new affiliation

01:27:07.670 --> 01:27:12.670
or an allegiance to some other system,

01:27:13.240 --> 01:27:14.623
religious or otherwise,

01:27:18.250 --> 01:27:20.180
but there's momentum.

01:27:26.380 --> 01:27:29.220
I do find it interesting that like,

01:27:29.220 --> 01:27:31.550
I still don't know where...

01:27:31.550 --> 01:27:32.410
Talk about momentum,

01:27:32.410 --> 01:27:36.970
COVID really kinda
truncated the experience.

01:27:36.970 --> 01:27:38.560
We put these things out there,

01:27:38.560 --> 01:27:40.133
there was a lot of response,

01:27:42.670 --> 01:27:44.930
I had to go on a hike and clear my head

01:27:44.930 --> 01:27:46.790
and figure out how to
deal with the fact that

01:27:46.790 --> 01:27:48.530
so many people, it turns out,

01:27:48.530 --> 01:27:51.560
really cared about the fact
that we talked about this.

01:27:51.560 --> 01:27:53.343
And they all didn't agree with us.

01:27:57.430 --> 01:28:01.573
But then COVID hit and it
kind of, in a lot of ways,

01:28:02.950 --> 01:28:05.092
it felt like it didn't happen.

01:28:05.092 --> 01:28:07.290
I had to get reacquainted
with the fact that like,

01:28:07.290 --> 01:28:09.250
remember January, February,

01:28:09.250 --> 01:28:12.020
this big milestone moment happened.

01:28:12.020 --> 01:28:15.120
And number two on our list.

01:28:15.120 --> 01:28:17.971
It seems like ages ago, I had
to get reacquainted with it.

01:28:17.971 --> 01:28:19.710
We had specifically, we
had done an interview

01:28:19.710 --> 01:28:24.710
for a major publication that
is related to Christian faith,

01:28:26.900 --> 01:28:30.803
that never was published
because COVID hit.

01:28:31.963 --> 01:28:35.613
And then we were featured
in another publication.

01:28:37.560 --> 01:28:40.450
Two pretty popular Christian publications

01:28:40.450 --> 01:28:42.423
were gonna do stories on this thing.

01:28:43.893 --> 01:28:44.840
And it just never happened.

01:28:44.840 --> 01:28:47.030
And the people who were talking about it

01:28:47.030 --> 01:28:49.230
had a whole lot of other
stuff to talk about.

01:28:49.230 --> 01:28:51.520
And maybe that was a blessing in disguise.

01:28:51.520 --> 01:28:55.023
I mean, again, one of the few times

01:28:55.023 --> 01:28:56.760
that I've written something in our medium

01:28:56.760 --> 01:28:59.820
was in response to the responses

01:28:59.820 --> 01:29:01.640
that we were processing at the time,

01:29:01.640 --> 01:29:03.840
the four of us, the two
of us and our wives.

01:29:08.021 --> 01:29:10.087
I have absolutely no regrets.

01:29:11.679 --> 01:29:14.840
Obviously, you always wish
you might've said something

01:29:14.840 --> 01:29:16.050
a little bit differently,

01:29:16.050 --> 01:29:18.390
'cause that's just the way it goes

01:29:18.390 --> 01:29:20.390
when you decide to talk about something,

01:29:22.290 --> 01:29:24.730
but the decision to share that story

01:29:26.060 --> 01:29:29.320
is something that I am just
incredibly grateful for.

01:29:29.320 --> 01:29:31.110
It was a coming out.

01:29:31.110 --> 01:29:32.943
It really was.
Yeah, 100%.

01:29:37.704 --> 01:29:39.247
It was so difficult to be a certain person

01:29:42.560 --> 01:29:44.960
and to be so open about so many things,

01:29:44.960 --> 01:29:49.890
but not be open about
something that's so core

01:29:49.890 --> 01:29:50.723
to who you are.

01:29:50.723 --> 01:29:52.170
Yeah.

01:29:52.170 --> 01:29:53.670
And that's why I think

01:29:53.670 --> 01:29:57.243
using that terminology is applicable.

01:30:01.230 --> 01:30:03.150
I'm not gonna say it's to the same degree

01:30:03.150 --> 01:30:05.550
or the same experience as somebody

01:30:06.410 --> 01:30:08.740
who's coming out of the closet would have,

01:30:08.740 --> 01:30:11.080
but like I can relate
at least a little bit.

01:30:11.080 --> 01:30:15.283
And it's because this is who I am.

01:30:16.696 --> 01:30:21.663
And I don't wanna be
ashamed or scared about it.

01:30:22.890 --> 01:30:26.220
I mean, that at its core, is that relief.

01:30:26.220 --> 01:30:30.470
Because it's like, hey, I'm
just being and openly sharing

01:30:30.470 --> 01:30:31.523
who I am.

01:30:32.990 --> 01:30:35.063
Take it as you will.

01:30:39.558 --> 01:30:41.570
Throughout our career,

01:30:41.570 --> 01:30:44.910
we've been people
pleasers in a lot of ways.

01:30:44.910 --> 01:30:47.793
It's like, we're pretty
tame, we're pretty safe.

01:30:50.730 --> 01:30:53.420
There's a lot of people from
a lot of different backgrounds

01:30:53.420 --> 01:30:55.090
that enjoy the things that we do.

01:30:55.090 --> 01:30:59.470
And we have a pretty
broad appeal by design.

01:30:59.470 --> 01:31:01.200
We want things to be accessible

01:31:01.200 --> 01:31:02.440
and we want it to be a break.

01:31:02.440 --> 01:31:05.950
We don't want it to be affiliated
with any particular view.

01:31:05.950 --> 01:31:08.720
We're just hey, just take a load off

01:31:08.720 --> 01:31:10.670
and come enjoy this thing that we made.

01:31:11.810 --> 01:31:14.750
But we didn't really take a stand

01:31:14.750 --> 01:31:16.320
as much as we just told our story,

01:31:16.320 --> 01:31:20.300
but it was interpreted as taking
a stand by a lot of people.

01:31:20.300 --> 01:31:23.720
And I don't think we've ever experienced

01:31:23.720 --> 01:31:26.860
that level of scrutiny and criticism.

01:31:26.860 --> 01:31:29.320
And that was something that
was very difficult at the time.

01:31:29.320 --> 01:31:32.990
But again, as someone who struggles with

01:31:35.420 --> 01:31:39.423
and places too much value on
other people's opinions of me,

01:31:41.020 --> 01:31:42.730
it's good to have those opinions

01:31:42.730 --> 01:31:46.510
be very, very loud and negative

01:31:46.510 --> 01:31:49.280
so that you can detach a little bit more

01:31:49.280 --> 01:31:50.890
from those expectations.

01:31:50.890 --> 01:31:52.310
Which kind of leads me into number one.

01:31:52.310 --> 01:31:54.630
Okay, we're two on number ones.

01:31:54.630 --> 01:31:57.750
Which I think, in some ways was,

01:31:57.750 --> 01:31:59.670
at least as 2020, as concerned,

01:31:59.670 --> 01:32:04.430
kind of a culmination of just

01:32:04.430 --> 01:32:05.550
kind of what you were getting at,

01:32:05.550 --> 01:32:09.730
which the beginning of,
sort of the next stage

01:32:09.730 --> 01:32:11.963
of what spirituality is to me.

01:32:13.037 --> 01:32:15.460
And I did a whole podcast on it.

01:32:15.460 --> 01:32:16.860
So, I'm not gonna go
into too many details,

01:32:16.860 --> 01:32:20.313
but it was my solo trip that
I took earlier in the year.

01:32:22.140 --> 01:32:27.140
And again, there were details
of things that happened to me

01:32:29.200 --> 01:32:33.410
sort of just things
that I kind of realized

01:32:33.410 --> 01:32:36.640
or came to grips with, whatever
the word you wanna use is,

01:32:36.640 --> 01:32:37.750
that I'm not going to share

01:32:37.750 --> 01:32:39.060
because I feel like it was for me,

01:32:39.060 --> 01:32:40.960
and I'm not trying to make it for you.

01:32:42.430 --> 01:32:44.730
But I think that it's very much tied

01:32:44.730 --> 01:32:46.050
to the fact that we told our stories

01:32:46.050 --> 01:32:49.860
because there was a little
bit of stagnation, right?

01:32:49.860 --> 01:32:51.820
Because there's this like,

01:32:51.820 --> 01:32:55.033
I've left this thing and I
don't know what I'm going to,

01:32:57.200 --> 01:33:01.030
but I don't want to jump

01:33:01.030 --> 01:33:03.960
into some other kind of
fundamentalism, right?

01:33:03.960 --> 01:33:06.520
I don't wanna jump from
one fundamentalism,

01:33:06.520 --> 01:33:10.720
from one ideological rut to another.

01:33:10.720 --> 01:33:15.320
Is just something that I was
trying really hard not to do.

01:33:15.320 --> 01:33:16.862
And it's very difficult to do that.

01:33:16.862 --> 01:33:21.862
It's very difficult to
maintain sort of an openness

01:33:22.050 --> 01:33:27.050
and an openness to spirituality in general

01:33:28.870 --> 01:33:29.730
when you kind of feel like

01:33:29.730 --> 01:33:31.483
you've sort of been duped in a way,

01:33:32.470 --> 01:33:34.060
but my trip which is something

01:33:34.060 --> 01:33:35.990
that I had been trying to organize,

